Description: share one open pull request page size between the listing and its guard
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

`gh pr list` returns 30 rows when no --limit is given, and it returns the newest
pull requests first, so a repository with more open pull requests than that
silently loses the older edges of the stack with no error anywhere. The listing
asked for 300 rows as a bare literal that nothing shared with the truncation
guard, so the two could drift and either side could start assuming the wrong page
size. The request now reads OPEN_PR_LIMIT, the same constant the guard compares
against, and a test drives a gh that truncates at 30 to pin the request.

diff --git a/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/scripts/watch-pr/github.test.ts b/pstack/skills/poteto-mode/scripts/watch-pr/github.test.ts
